00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.720
MILLION COLOR!

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.180
TURNS!

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.810
<i>I'm worried since I'm currently unsure of where the Willgem is.</i>

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:32.690
<i>However, being on the moon for the first time in over two years... has given me a chance to finally relax.</i>

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:42.490
<i>Without that, I don't think I'd be able to handle being forced to continually pilot Mobile Suits and fight.</i>

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:54.510
<b>Determined To Fight</b>

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.600
Are you sure we'll be alright?

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.690
Those who are on patrol never tend to look in this passage.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.820
Why didn't you know about that, Loran?

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:20.110
I never ventured to this part of Genganam very often when I was younger.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:27.330
Are you sure you still wish to meet with this "Agrippa" person?

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:30.710
The man who's been forcibly managing the lives of everyone living here...

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:34.630
...as well as Gym Ghingnham, are people with whom I must meet.

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:38.220
This is Queen Dianna's city...

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.530
Miashei, please handle those carefully.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.820
Don't forget the ones that look like medical supplies!

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:06.410
We went to all this trouble to swipe them. We've got move carefully and keep quiet!

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.410
Mechanical Dolls! Everybody, hide!

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.000
It looks like a patrol came this way earlier than expected.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.920
Do you think they suspect us?

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.600
What the... Isn't that the White Doll and a Kapool!?

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.720
Colonel Michael!

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.730
What are all of you doing here?

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:32.020
- Sochie!
- Miashei!

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.520
I'm relieved we've found one another under such good circumstances!

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.900
So am I!

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.610
You're still looking as good as always!

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:40.610
And you're looking as young and vibrant as ever!

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.820
Hmm... you're still doing fine too, Queen Dianna?

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.700
Yep. Thanks for asking.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.910
- Hurry it up!
- In that case, allow me to help you carry those.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:51.910
Well, we seem to be short on most of our supplies after completing our journey.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:56.420
Exactly. I'm sure the Queen won't mind if you take some of these supplies.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.710
- Really, now?
- Stupid, isn't it?

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:03.720
Then you must be the true Dianna Soriel.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.220
She is indeed Queen Dianna.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.300
I thank you for your hospitality.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.600
You're the real deal!? I can't believe it!

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.810
Then, where would Lady Kihel currently be?

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.730
Wouldn't she be with Harry?

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:18.190
In that case, there's no need to worry, Sir Guin.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.530
It's about time for the meeting which we were promised.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:22.110
So we should get ready.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:25.820
We'll be traveling to their so-called White Palace.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:29.120
Do you have a meeting set up with Agrippa Maintainer?

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.500
Correct. It wouldn't have been possible without Lady Lily's diplomatic skills.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.500
Just what should be expected of a nobleman's daughter!

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:39.500
You were able to punch directly through the White Palace's bureaucracy.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:44.220
People born of a noble lineage all tend to think the same way.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:48.100
But the first time Agrippa saw me...

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.600
He was so forward, he couldn't even keep his eyes off me.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:56.020
His crudeness makes my skin crawl... Ugh... every time I think about it!

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:58.400
I realize that it must have been difficult.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:02.190
Let's be sure to move quickly, before they decide to change their feelings on this matter.

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:05.110
- Then, let's all go together!
- Me too?

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.410
Anyone can tell you also wanted to meet with him, right?

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.990
You're as sharp as ever, Lady Lily Borjarno...

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:26.430
We might be going to the White Palace...

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.430
...But OUR one and only castle is the Willgem.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.720
Be sure to defend it for us.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:31.510
You can rely on me.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:35.520
And while we're gone, make sure they hurry and get the supplies loaded.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.100
I'll be sure to do that.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:39.810
Lady Lily..!

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:41.020
Sorry about that.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:45.900
Also, if you find any of their famed Cocoa in the supplies, please get out a can for me.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:47.320
I'll do that.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.700
We're off.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:55.200
Do you think they'll be okay without bodyguards?

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:59.000
Lady Lily rejected the idea of a Borjarnon escort.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.630
Isn't it odd to use an umbrella as a diplomatic ambassador's symbol?

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:03.800
I think it's odd too.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:16.520
Yet another set of negotiations with a different leader. Do you think it'll work out?

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.230
Well, this time, they'll be hearing about Duke Borjarno's true intentions instead.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:24.690
It's more important that we find out who the current leader of the Moon truly is.

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:35.830
Was there something you needed?

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.120
No, nothing.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:41.130
Sometimes, a person finds themselves disliking the very task they have no choice but to carry out.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:42.500
Oh, I see.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:45.300
Have you ever felt that way?

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.300
- Yes, I know what you mean.
- Do you?

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:55.720
I'm tired of having to take advantage of my own people.

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:01.020
Hmm? Lieutenant, What is it?
- We're leaving.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.900
We gain nothing from having you stay here.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:06.530
Forgive me, I haven't been of much assistance.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:07.690
Let's go.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.900
Take this, you damn White Mustache!

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:11.320
Quit holding out on me!

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:13.490
What good do you think deploying on your own will do?

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:15.200
This is a real war!

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:21.620
Damn it, that White Mustache treats the Moonrace like childish pupas in a cocoon!

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.290
All I have to do is think about its name...

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:26.710
...and then even my very DNA begins to boil!

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:30.720
Come on!

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:43.900
Is this their welcoming party?

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:45.020
An Escort service?

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:51.200
The House of Maintainer's symbol has been added to these palace vehicles...

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:55.620
Hmm, How do you think they make that thing move?

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:58.620
Hide your ignorance! Pretend like you already know how it works.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:01.290
We don't have any idea what'd happen if they started to view us as inferior...

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:04.000
But still...that's such a smooth looking vehicle.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:07.130
Our technology for electric automobiles has advanced to this point.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.720
Ahh, there's my home!

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:19.100
Did you always intend to eventually return here?

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.890
That's...

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:23.100
Well, it's still where my home was...

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.600
That's true, of course.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:33.200
Thank you for your assistance, Sir Guin.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.110
It's nothing.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:36.110
That place is pretty smooth looking as well.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:37.490
It's fairly sturdy looking!

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:49.800
The House of Maintainer's symbol was even placed on my Palace...

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:54.220
It's the enemy's mechanical dolls!

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:57.220
Mechanical Dolls? Doesn't that seem odd?

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:00.890
This place is a port! They wouldn't seriously try to attack us here!

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:03.310
No, The Mahiroo team would do it.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:06.600
The Ghingnham troops don't exactly have a commendable reputation among the Moonrace.

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:08.810
Why would they be like that!?

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:12.190
History speaks for itself. I can't change that.

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:21.200
All of you, remember that we're still inside Genganam's port. Our objective is to blast the Earth's ship into chopped sushi bits!

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.910
However, make sure you leave the White Mustache for me!

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:28.290
Please don't use any of the beam weapons!

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:32.210
Mr. Ames and Mr. John are never here at critical times like these!

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.930
Think you can survive one of my direct tackles!?

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:40.930
This one's...

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.100
He overpowered my strike!

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.530
These people are part of the Moonrace!?

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:55.900
Our barrage is too thin...

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:57.700
Prepare to move the ship!

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.820
But then we'll become a target!

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:01.200
We already are one!

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.200
I'll head into the city...

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.200
The city!?

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:04.490
The city can act as our shield.

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:14.130
We're starting to tilt!

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:16.510
Mr. Jacop, try to keep the ship level!

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.520
Her Majesty, Dianna has finally returned.

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:30.100
But, she's here with those Terrans!

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.110
This one must be the rumored duplicate.

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:35.320
According to the data, she's 2 kilograms heavier than she was before.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.900
She's the duplicate.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:40.320
I've never seen a building constructed in this manner before.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:45.990
That's right, something such as this would be new for you, Guin.

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:51.210
Lady Lily Borjarno, I've been waiting quite awhile for your arrival!

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:52.420
How do you do?

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:54.290
l am Guin Sard Rhineford...

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:57.210
I give you my thanks for granting us this opportunity to meet with you.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:58.920
Of course.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:02.800
I'm quite pleased to finally be able to meet with Lily Borjarno.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.810
Oh, and could she perhaps be...

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:09.890
Yes. This girl is my secretary, Miss Kihel Heim.

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:13.610
I expect that you were quite surprised by her appearance, Highness.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:19.700
When we first saw the Queen of the Moon, we too had the same reaction that you did.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:22.320
They both look very much alike.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:28.330
On the earth, I had to endure quite a bit of trouble because I resembled Dianna.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:34.630
Lady Lily, your good mood makes your lovely skin shine brighter than ever before!

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:36.880
Thank you very much, Highness.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:46.720
Impressive!

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:49.390
Sir Guin, if you would, please step forward with your secretary as well.

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:56.310
You missed!

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:58.530
Guess I fell for it...

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:11.540
What is the Mahiroo team doing in the city!?

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:12.410
What the...!?

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:14.500
It's that ship!

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:17.210
Don't, Bruno! We can't let the city get damaged!

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:20.210
At this rate, we won't be able to keep up our defenses.

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:22.420
If this continues, the city's gonna be destroyed!

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:25.800
Can somebody else please take over this unit for me!?

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:27.890
Letting them leave the port was a mistake!

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:33.890
Bruno, take the ship over to the palace!

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:35.400
Great idea!

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:40.110
If we use the leader of the Moonrace as a shield, they can't possibly attack us!

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:44.400
So Lady Lily's father is a very powerful man, isn't he?
- Yes.

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:47.780
Once Duke Borjarno unites the continent of Ameria...

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:50.080
...he still wishes to have peaceful relations with us here?

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:54.080
The Moon's always been ruled by a Queen. He wishes to convert it into a King's legacy!

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:59.000
- A spaceship!?
- It's the Terran ship!
- The Mahiroo Team is here!?

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:07.180
That spacecraft intends to land here!?

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:08.390
They're here?

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:11.810
- Lord Guin, it's too dangerous!
- What's going on!?

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:16.600
Willgem has escaped to this place!

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:20.110
Who's using my Borjarnon!?

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:30.080
My poor palace!

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:34.080
How could they bring that dreaded war to this place!?

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:35.500
He's scary...

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:39.080
Why do you think this is happening?

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:42.210
This is happening because they used a man from the Ghingnham lineage.

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:44.670
People like him simply cannot understand the consequences of that choice.

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:47.090
Ahh, now that I can see!

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:50.010
Have Gym Ghingnham protect my palace!

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:51.300
Will you have any use for him?

00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:53.810
Frankly, he's a bit too simple-minded.

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:57.100
Once again...

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:01.110
Alright!

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:02.770
- Lord Guin!
-That's not good!

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:05.490
There's too much rope!

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:06.900
Pull me up!

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:11.990
I cannot allow this to damage the palace...

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.790
You'd better fight me!

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:17.710
I'm coming for you, bastard!

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.000
If that's what you're planning...

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:31.010
Are you people trying to ruin our negotiations!?

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:34.970
The mechanical dolls ambushed us and we were left without any other options!

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:38.180
This was the only way that we could protect the Willgem.

00:14:38.180 --> 00:14:40.400
Neither side can use their weapons down here!

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:42.190
It's a tightly packed underground city.

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:43.980
Bruno, begin the landing procedures!

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:44.770
Right!

00:14:44.770 --> 00:14:48.190
Was this a trap set by the palace officials?

00:14:48.190 --> 00:14:50.200
No, I don't believe so.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:53.200
Still, there's no doubt that the Moonrace was behind this.

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:56.200
True. Gym Ghingnham, and Agrippa...

00:14:56.200 --> 00:15:00.870
I'm betting I can use this situation as a weapon to turn the negotiations in our favor.

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:02.710
Everyone, I have a plan. Protect the ship!

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.090
Lieutenant!

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:12.090
It wasn't your skills that won this fight!

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:15.390
But rather, it was the strength of that machine!

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:18.680
Let me use that suit! I dare you to fight with the same model we use!

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:20.480
- Stop this!
- Let go of me!

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:25.610
If you were to put up a fight here, it would only result in the destruction of Queen Dianna's Palace!

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:27.610
I know that...!

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:31.910
Capture their patrol vehicles as well!

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:35.410
No way! You haven't beaten us yet!

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:41.370
Not only did they bring their battleship to my Palace, but they brought that White Mobile Suit as well!

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:42.710
"Turn A"

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:48.710
Duke Borjarno's letter promised us that his only intention was ensuring peaceful relations!

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:51.590
Correct. My father did not lie to you.

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:53.300
Despite the situation we see before us!?

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:58.810
Naturally. If we came to wage war, then we wouldn'tve traveled here with the lone Willgem.

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:00.680
We would've used a full fleet of ships!

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:02.480
Is that so?

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:05.480
In that case, would you care to have a room to rest in the palace?

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:09.400
Dianna, or Kihel...

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:12.490
There wouldn't happen to be a special doll for our use in the Palace?

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:16.490
This Palace is only used for administration, paperwork, and as a place to reside.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:19.200
How'd it go?

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:23.210
Agrippa says he'll overlook things if our Mechanical Dolls leave the premise.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:26.290
He fears the Mustached Mobile Suit, doesn't he?

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:30.210
Correct. He says it can be none other than the "Turn A".

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:31.510
What is that?

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:33.170
The marking on the Mustache's face...

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:37.100
Appears to be an "A", but flipped upside down. One can read that symbol as "Turn A".

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:38.890
In that case...

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:43.600
Was this "Turn A" ever referenced in the chronicles of the Dark History?

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:46.100
The Dark History?

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:50.690
Well, as far as I've heard... no, it wasn't.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:56.570
Everyone, report to the briefing room. We will be planning our next engagement.

00:16:56.570 --> 00:17:00.160
Something has happened. Ghingnham seems unusually concerned.

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:03.410
Go and take care of the situation down there.

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:04.370
Sir!

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:05.710
Gym Ghingnham...

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:10.380
If you knew "Turn A" had been uncovered, why did you allow the Mahiroo troops to run about unchecked!?

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:11.710
The Turn A, you say?

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:14.670
It's the Earthling's white Mobile Suit!

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:18.300
You've suspected the same thing, haven't you, Agrippa?

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:20.510
That is exactly why I've had to use whatever methods are necessary.

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:21.890
But...!

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:24.310
- Explain it to him.
- Sir!

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:27.900
The third airlock is opening! Gold type SUMO Launching!

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:29.190
Damn that Harry...

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:30.480
Leave him.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:34.190
He's probably gone off to personally greet Agrippa.

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:55.800
What are you doing?

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:59.390
We're taking an alternate route into Genganam.

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:01.680
However, this isn't a route I've used very frequently.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:11.980
Is something wrong?

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:16.900
I never knew that there were any Mobile Suits in use here...

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:28.210
I've never seen that Mobile Suit before.

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:30.790
This location reminds me of a Mountain Cycle.

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:32.090
A Mountain Cycle?

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:36.590
You're being unreasonable!

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:38.090
We're not leaving until we're done!

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:39.880
We have to defeat that Mustache...

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:42.390
Or else my DNA will never be satisfied!

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:47.100
Then I will grant you the means to achieve your satisfaction, Sweatson.

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:48.600
General!

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:50.630
I will forgive your transgressions if you succeed here.

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:51.190
Of course!

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:59.200
Bastards! So you want to turn this location into a war zone after all?

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.860
Milady... Mr. Jacop!

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:04.280
These guys are even more reckless than Dianna Counter!

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:07.290
And to think they're supposed to be considered pros!

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:10.210
- There are less than ten machines...
- It'll be enough.

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:14.210
Has Agrippa Maintainer decided to break off the negotiations?

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:19.300
Listen up, earthlings!

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:21.300
Hand over the White Mustache.

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:25.810
Otherwise, your three friends in the palace will be executed!

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:29.180
How could you possibly use such a tactic!?

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:31.600
We must hand over White Doll?

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:33.190
There's no way we can do that!

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:35.400
They intend to kill Sir Guin and the others?

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:39.400
We came here to conduct peace talks! What's the meaning of these threats!?

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:42.410
This order did not come from me.

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:44.410
You've been lying to us!

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:46.200
I'm as confused as you are.

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:49.200
You had no intention of negotiating from the very start.

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:50.910
You deceived all of us.

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:52.580
That's not true!

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:54.000
Your deceitful stance...

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:56.710
All that you're going to do is repeat the Dark History!

00:19:56.710 --> 00:19:59.590
Do you honestly wish for such mistakes to be repeated?

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:02.880
I can't expect one of earth's common citizens to understand.

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:07.510
Even when a civilian has seen the unhappiness the Dark History brings to humanity...

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:08.970
...anybody can see that it's a thing to be feared!

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:10.890
The Dark History?

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:13.900
You seem fairly familiar with the Dark History.

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:16.690
I know a bit about its beginnings.

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:21.110
Surely, you've heard of the terrible history that was the Earth's "Turn A", and the Moon's "Turn X".

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:26.200
Together, they both carry the burden of the disgusting history that brought about mankind's greatest loss.

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:28.490
- Turn A?
- Turn X?

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:33.370
Perhaps that's why you've been arguing with Gym Ghingnham recently?

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:38.000
I request that you please refrain from inquiring about our internal problems.

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:43.170
The White Doll's been like our special guardian angel!

00:20:43.170 --> 00:20:47.100
If we give in to their demands, we'll be signing our own death warrant!

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:51.890
And if Sir Guin, Lady Lily and even Queen Dianna were killed because of it?

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:53.600
Don't discuss that possibility!

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:55.190
Okay...

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:58.270
I'll give you half an hour to debate this.

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:01.190
Then at that point, you must hand the Mustache over to us!

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:11.080
If that really was a Mountain Cycle for the moon, then...

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:14.290
...shouldn't attacking it have been a priority?

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:19.880
No. We must first ensure that Queen Dianna's still safe.

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:24.510
We're not the only one's who've been taken hostage here, they've threatened the entire palace!

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:27.090
You can't just let yourself stew over it.

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:30.180
We still need to conduct our negotiations.

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:32.390
That may be so, however...

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:34.310
I don't know what to do next.

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:36.190
Oh? Is that so?

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:41.110
Both Agrippa and yourself want the same thing... this "Turn A", or rather, our Mustached Doll.

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:42.400
Correct.

00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:45.490
But, Loran is not simply going to hand it over to them very easily.

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:48.200
At least not without us ordering him to do it.

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:54.410
I see! Our Mustached Mechanical Doll is what they're referring to as "Turn A"...But what does it mean?

00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:56.790
I'm afraid I don't know either.

00:21:58.080 --> 00:21:59.580
Midgard!

00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:37.540
<b><i>Yama no ha tsuki wa michi</i></b>

00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:37.540
<b>As the full moon, casts itself over the mountain's edge...</b>

00:22:37.540 --> 00:22:44.590
<b><i>iki zuku anata no mori</i></b>

00:22:37.540 --> 00:22:44.590
<b>...it spreads the breath of life spreads into the forest where you stand...</b>

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:51.720
<b><i>Natsu kusa abite nemuru</i></b>

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:51.720
<b>As you sleep in the summer grass...</b>

00:22:51.760 --> 00:22:58.600
<b><i>Itooshii yokogao</i></b>

00:22:51.760 --> 00:22:58.600
<b>...your profile is a lovely sight to behold.</b>

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:06.690
<b><i>Kaze ni</i></b>

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:06.690
<b>The wind...</b>

00:23:06.690 --> 00:23:13.780
<b><i>LaLaLu... LaLaLu...</i></b>

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:20.670
<b><i>utae... hane ni</i></b>

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:20.670
<b>The sight of your wings, is seen...</b>

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:25.170
<b><i>tsuki utsushi</i></b>

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:25.170
<b>...in the moon's reflection.</b>

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:32.800
<b><i>Inochi kagaya kase yo</i></b>

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:32.800
<b>This wonderful life will shine vividly.</b>

00:23:40.410 --> 00:23:45.730
<i>Ghingnham has excavated the Turn X from the lunar Mountain Cycle.</i>

00:23:46.690 --> 00:23:50.610
<i>Agrippa wishes to prevent the White Doll from calling out to the Turn X.</i>

00:23:51.530 --> 00:23:54.200
<i>And in order to expose the truth of the Dark History...</i>

00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:56.200
<i>...Queen Dianna heads for the Winter Palace.</i>

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:02.580
<i>Next time... on </i>TURN A GUNDAM...<i>
Turn X Activated</i>

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:08.420
<b>Turn X Activated</b>

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:05.290
"Another wind has awoken."
